      "content": "so you're saying that intimidating the soviets and securing a geopolitical advantage was actually just as important as ending the war? that seems like a huge moral leap to make—that killing hundreds of thousands of civilians in cities is a justifiable way to win a political power struggle or prevent a future influence shift. isn't that just accepting that mass civilian deaths are okay as long as they serve certain national interests?",
